# Keep committed patch-package patches byte-identical across checkout on this
# core.autocrlf=true repo. Without this, a fresh clone re-smudges the .patch to
# CRLF and patch-package fails to re-apply. `-text` (not `binary`) stops EOL
# conversion while keeping the patch diffable for review.
#
# Scoped to patches/**/*.patch — a path that matches nothing that exists today
# (patches are net-new), so zero working-tree churn. This does NOT pre-empt the
# deferred repo-wide .gitattributes question (Tier-4 #30), which is about churn
# across the whole existing tree.
patches/**/*.patch -text
